---
title: Detached start · pool boot ended
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    classDef ok stroke-width:1.6px
    classDef wait stroke-width:1.6px
    classDef fail stroke-width:1.6px

    [*] --> watching : boot recorded
    watching --> watching : every 1 s, boot alive
    watching --> ended : [boot ended]
    state ended <<choice>>
    ended --> exit : [ready, not stopping]
    ended --> grace : [starting or stopping]
    grace --> exit : 10 s passed
    grace --> done : [start finished]
    exit --> gone
    gone --> recovered : next up proves it gone
    grace --> waited : a new up arrives
    waited --> gone : owner exited, ≤15 s
    done --> [*]
    recovered --> [*]

    note right of exit
        Same as a crash: marker
        released, process exits.
    end note
    note left of gone
        The next up waits for this,
        then recovers the run.
    end note
    note right of waited
        Only while the pool record
        shows the pool stopped.
        One line says so.
    end note

    class recovered ok
    class grace wait
    class exit fail
